  "title": "Illusionism",
  "role": "model",
  "summary": "Illusionism, as named by Keith Frankish and long defended by Daniel C. Dennett: phenomenal consciousness is an introspective illusion. Experiences have no qualitative feels, introspection misrepresents them as having such feels, and the task is the illusion problem, explaining why the illusion arises and why it is so powerful, in place of the hard problem.",
